IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa15-nouns.l4: the types that more than one chapter module of coa15 (Part 18, ss 658 to 737, lines 8745-9668 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt) shares. DECLARE only: no rules, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT. Every type, constructor and field begins with
-- the label of the provision where its concept first arises (the Act's own numbering), as the keel's naming rule says.
-- Types a single chapter uses are declared in that chapter's module.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.

-- The person an offence section charges. Almost every offence in Part 18 reads "an offence is committed by (a) the
-- company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default"; s 715 charges "every director who is in default".
-- src:8750 | (2) If a company purports to act in contravention of this section—
-- src:8751 | (a) an offence is committed by—
-- src:8752 | (i) the company, and
-- src:8753 | (ii) every officer of the company who is in default, and
-- src:8754 | (b) the purported acquisition is void.
@ref s 658(2) Offence by the company and by every officer in default (src:8750-8754)
DECLARE `s 658(2) person charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 658(2) the company`
    `s 658(2) an officer of the company`
    `s 658(2) a director of the company`
    `s 658(2) any other person`

-- The statement of capital that ss 663(3), 689(3), 708(3), 720B(2) and 730(5) each require in the same five words.
-- A witness can say which items the statement states; whether that suffices is the rule of each section.
-- src:8823 | (3) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital immediately following the cancellation—
-- src:8824 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:8825 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:8826 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:8827 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:8828 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:8829 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:8830 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
-- src:8831 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 663(3) Content of the statement of capital (src:8823-8831)
DECLARE `s 663(3) class entry` HAS
    `s 663(3) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 663(3) statement of capital` HAS
    `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 663(3) states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 663(3) entries for the classes of shares` IS A LIST OF `s 663(3) class entry`

-- "the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences" (ss 707(7)
-- and 728(5)): the core's `Fine limit` has no constructor for "the greater of" two amounts, so the two sections share this one.
-- NEEDS-CORE.md records it.
-- src:9300 | (b) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 707(7) The daily default fine limit in the two wordings of the text (src:9300-9300)
DECLARE `s 707(7) daily default fine limit` IS ONE OF
    `s 707(7) one-tenth of the statutory maximum`
    `s 707(7) one-tenth of the greater of an amount in pounds and the amount corresponding to a level on the standard scale`
        HAS `s 707(7) amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER, `s 707(7) level on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER

-- The penalty of ss 707(7) and 728(5): the core's `Penalty` carries its daily default fine as a core `Fine limit`, which cannot say
-- "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4"; this record carries the daily limit as the type above.
-- src:9298 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:9299 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:9300 | (b) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 707(7) Penalty on conviction for the offence of failing to make the return (src:9298-9300)
DECLARE `s 707(7) penalty` HAS
    `s 707(7) how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
    `s 707(7) fine not exceeding` IS A MAYBE `Fine limit`
    `s 707(7) daily default fine for continued contravention not exceeding` IS A MAYBE `s 707(7) daily default fine limit`
